      explanation: "Rhizobium, Nitrosomonas, and Nitrobacter are crucial in the nitrogen cycle. Rhizobium fixes atmospheric nitrogen into usable forms for plants through symbiosis with legumes. Nitrosomonas converts ammonia to nitrites, and Nitrobacter converts nitrites to nitrates, which are absorbed by plants.",
