      explanation: "The Sepoy Mutiny of 1857 began at Meerut on 10 May 1857, when soldiers rebelled against the British East India Company over grievances. They marched to Delhi to seek support from the Mughal emperor Bahadur Shah II, marking a significant moment in India's struggle for independence.",
